# Nebula Aura Theme for PI-Desktop — third-party notice

This plugin is a **PI-Desktop port**. The colour values (surface, text, accent,
semantic and selection colours) are derived from:

> **Nebula Aura Theme** — a modern light, dark, violet and midnight theme pack
> for VS Code, Cursor and Antigravity.
> Copyright (c) Luis Penholato
> https://github.com/luismpenholato/nebula-aura-theme
> Licensed under the MIT License.

No source file, artwork or VS Code theme JSON from that repository is
redistributed here. The port re-targets the palette onto PI-Desktop's own
`--ds-*` design tokens and writes new CSS; a small number of colours were
adjusted away from the source values so that text keeps WCAG-legible contrast
against each base background (see README for which).

## Fonts - referenced, never shipped

This package contains **no font files**. The `--font-sans` stack names two
families that the user installs on their own machine:

  * **Maple Mono NF** — subframe7536, https://github.com/subframe7536/maple-font,
    Copyright 2022 The Maple Mono Project Authors, **SIL Open Font License 1.1**
    (`OS/2.fsType = 0x0000`, Installable). Take the `Maple Mono NF` release asset.
  * **腾祥爱情体简** — 腾祥字型, https://www.tensentype.com, free for personal use.
    Its installed family name is `Tensentype AiQingJ` and its `OS/2.fsType` is
    `0x0008` (Editable embedding). Windows resolves the Chinese name too, so no
    `@font-face` alias is needed (verified: pixel-identical canvas renders for
    both spellings, and both differ from the monospace fallback).

Releases 1.1.0 and 1.2.0 bundled woff2 copies instead. 1.2.0 pushed one theme's
declared assets past the host's 4 MiB **total** cap, which made the host drop
every asset and reject each `url()`, so the theme rendered with a fallback font;
and bundling 腾祥爱情体简 at all rested on a personal-use judgement rather than on
a redistribution grant inside the file (it embeds no licence text — nameID 13/14
absent). Release 1.3.0 ships nothing, so neither question is open any more: the
only third-party content left in this package is the colour palette credited
above, and each user's own font install is governed by that font's licence.

## Adapted plugins (referenced, not redistributed)

Release 1.5.0 adds colour mappings for two plugins from the official marketplace
repository [`vastsa/pi-desktop-plugins`](https://github.com/vastsa/pi-desktop-plugins)
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 vastsa): `pi.gitlens` 0.2.7 and `pi.file-manager` 0.3.1.
Nothing from those plugins is copied here — no JS, no CSS, no manifest, no asset. The
theme only writes their *public* CSS custom-property names (`--bg`, `--fg`,
`--surface-raised`, `--accent`, ...) and the class names they render with
(`.segmented`, `.tree-size`), which is interface-level knowledge needed to interoperate,
the same way the host's `--ds-*` tokens are used. Any plugin that does not consume the
`pluginTheme` payload the host offers simply keeps its own colours (see README).

